# cw107, the under-breath counter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw107
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_fh_marl_cragpeak
written_by claude-codex-cw-1
title the under-breath counter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=chatty humour=merry
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk counts_things_under_the_breath
likes crisp_apples old_tales new_boots summer_evenings
dislikes waiting rats
fears a_count_that_stops a_closed_workroom
hopes a_better_place_at_the_loom work_with_a_future
topics work +0.5 pastimes +0.4 memories +0.3 prices +0.3 friends +0.2 faith -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=merry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# counts #passes# under the breath, tells a #tale# with a grin, and keeps one eye on the next chance to move ahead.

words
oath! = Six and seven | By the skipped count
saying! = Leave room for the next turn | A count can start again
count = count | tally
numbers = numbers | little figures
passes = shuttle passes | crossings of the thread
shuttle = shuttle | wooden runner
loom = loom | weaving frame
mark = mark | pencil notch
wool = wool | fleece
bell = bell | early bell
thread = thread | strand
row = row | line of weaving
cloth = cloth | woven length
edge = edge | firm border
bench = bench | work seat
hour = hour | hour of work
hours = hours | hours at work
rows = rows | lines of weaving
apple = apple | orchard apple
tale = tale | well-told story
boots = boots | stout boots
evening = evening | long light after supper
wait = wait | pause with nothing to do
door = door | workroom door
rat = rat | grey rat
mine = mine | deep shaft
stone = stone | loose rock
step = step
steps = steps | paces
coin = coin | day's pay
road = road | lake road
word = word | report
seat = seat | place to sit
hand = hand | working paw
hands = hands | working paws

any
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : A day away from the #loom# gives us a #tale# to take back. | I can dance as long as these #boots# hold me.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : A seller counts every #coin# except the worker's. | I would show the maker's #hour# beside the shop's price.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : A House can see the #cloth# and miss the #hands# behind it. | I will not thank a crest for letting me keep my #bench#.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : There is work for one more #hand# only if someone makes room. | I would teach a newcomer the #loom#; I would also ask who pays the wage.
opinion @1 church against 1 : A sermon takes an #hour# that could put bread on a table. | I have heard good words there, but the #loom# still needs hands.
opinion @1 drink for 1 : A jar after the #shuttle# rests can turn a poor day around. | I like a #tale# better when a friend has something to sip.
opinion @1 times against 1 : The #coin# buys less with every turn of the #count#. | I work another #hour# and still find the purse thin.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The #road# can take a wolf toward better work or bring a late cart. | I would walk it in these #boots# if the offer were sound.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. One, two—there you are. | #greet#. I have a #tale# if you have an #hour#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Do not mind my #count#; I am listening. | #greet#. A new face makes the #hour# pass faster.
line @3 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Let me finish this #row#. | #greet#. My #shuttle# is moving, but I can hear you.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. I have already counted the first #passes#. | #greet#. These #boots# beat the bell here.
line @5 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. The #evening# has run ahead of my #count#. | #greet#. I left the #loom# where tomorrow can find it.
line @1 greet.return : #welcome_back#. I have reached the next #row#. | You returned before I lost the #count#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Sit by my #bench# and tell me your news. | I saved the sharper #apple# for you.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come along; there is a #seat# here. | You know where I keep the #apple# basket.
line @1 again.open : Twice today? I shall add you to the #count#. | Back so soon; the #shuttle# has only crossed once.
line @1 farewell : #saying.capitalize#. Keep moving. | #farewell#. Mind the #stone# near the gate.
line @1 farewell.return : Another #tale# next time. | I will keep a #seat# if you come back.
line @1 react.news : #listen.capitalize#. I nearly lost my #count#. | That stopped the #shuttle#. Go on.
line @1 react.news.new : Fresh news. Where did the first #word# come from? | I had not counted on that. Who saw it?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a piece of the #tale# earlier. | So the #count# comes out as I thought.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That #count# skips a step. Who checked it? | A neat #tale# can hide a loose #thread#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That hurts to hear. I shall set the #shuttle# down and stay. | That is a heavy #tale#. Sit with me.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good! That belongs in a bright #tale#. | A happy turn; I shall count that among the good days.
line @1 answer.how : Counting the #passes# and making plans. | Well enough. These #boots# have another day in them.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : My #shuttle# has not stopped since dawn. | Busy. The #rows# keep coming.
line @1 ask.how : How is your #hour# going? | Have these #boots# carried you far today?
line @1 sympathise : I can put down the #count# and hear you. | We can take a #seat# until you want to speak.
line @1 reassure : A missed #row# is a reason to begin it again. | You have another #step# after this one.
line @1 decline : I cannot spare the #hour#; the #cloth# must be finished. | I would take it on, but my #count# is full today.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair. I shall ask another #hand#. | You have answered; I will mark the #count# complete.
line @1 thank : You gave me back an #hour#. Thank you. | I owe you an #apple# for that help.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was one #step#, nothing more. | I had a free #hand#; take the help.
line @1 preclose : One more #row# before I leave this #bench#. | The #shuttle# is waiting for my return.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : I counted your moves; you missed one. | Those #boots# are loud enough to announce a trick.
line @1 tease.return [pair.band=friends] : I will put that in my next #tale#. | You are ahead by one; I have the next #step#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. Let me add it to the #count#. | #bc_fair_enough#. Another #row# then.
line @1 give.advice : Count the #hours# before you promise them. | Keep a #seat# for yourself when everyone else asks.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Take the busy #road# until the trouble passes. | Do not let an empty #road# shorten your journey tonight.
scene whispered_count
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #passes# low enough that only I can hear. | The #numbers# come out of my mouth before I know it.
b : Does it help you keep your place? | Do others mind?
a : Yes. If I stop, I know where I lost the #row#. | Some smile. The #shuttle# is louder than I am.

scene lost_place
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I once missed a #count# because someone called from the door. | A broken #row# sends me back to the last sure place.
b : Did you start over? | Is that a great loss?
a : From the last #mark#, not the beginning. | An #hour# at worst. Better than a crooked length.

scene waiting_cart
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I can finish three #rows# while a cart keeps us waiting. | Standing by the #door# does not make the #wool# come sooner.
b : Do you keep working then? | Does waiting make you restless?
a : If there is #thread# enough, yes. | It does. I need a #count# to keep my paws busy.

scene better_place
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I want work that gives me a new #row# to learn, not only the old one. | A #bench# with more responsibility would suit me.
b : Have you asked for it? | Would you leave this place?
a : I will, when I can show the #cloth# to back the request. | For fair #coin# and work I could grow in, perhaps.

scene sharp_apple
when topic=food here.season=summer|autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like an #apple# with enough bite to make me blink. | The crisp #apple# goes first in my basket.
b : Are the sour ones wasted? | Do you save any?
a : No. They wake me better than the #bell#. | One for after the #loom# stops.

scene old_tale_turn
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A good #tale# waits before its best turn. | I know a #tale# is working when someone asks me to slow down.
b : Do you ever change the ending? | Do you slow down?
a : Only if I say it is a new telling. | For one #step#, then I make them wait again.

scene new_boot_noise
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #boots# announce me before I reach the #door#. | I walked the #road# in #boots# that still squeaked.
b : Does that bother you? | Will they quiet down?
a : No. At least no one can say I crept in. | After enough #steps#. I am keeping count.

scene long_evening
when topic=weather here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #evening# gives me time for one more #tale#. | I can finish a #row# and still see light at the window.
b : Will you work all evening? | What will you do afterward?
a : No. Even I stop when the #shuttle# has had enough. | Walk until the #boots# take me home.

scene rat_in_shed
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I heard a #rat# behind the #bench# and counted the scratching. | A #rat# can make a mess of stored #thread#.
b : Did you find it? | How will you protect the thread?
a : No. I found the gap by the #door# instead. | Keep it above the floor and close that gap.

scene mine_warning
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I do not like work that sends a wolf below loose #stone# without a check. | A #mine# needs more than a hopeful word about safety.
b : Have you seen such a place? | What would you demand?
a : Enough to know a missing brace is not a small matter. | A sound beam, a clear way out, and someone counting the #hands#.

scene festival_steps
when topic=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I can keep a dance #count# even when the music hurries. | The festival makes these #boots# earn their leather.
b : Do you lead? | Do you dance long?
a : If nobody else starts, yes. | Until I miss the #step# and laugh about it.

scene short_pay
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A short #coin# at week's end makes every #hour# feel longer. | I write my #hours# down, though I remember the #count#.
b : Have you challenged a short wage? | Why write it down?
a : When the #mark# was wrong, yes. | A written #count# is easier to show another wolf.

scene friend_tale
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# hears the part of my #tale# I have polished too much. | I can finish an #hour# faster when I know a friend waits afterward.
b : Does your friend correct you? | Do you meet after work?
a : Yes. That is how the #tale# stays worth telling. | When we can. I bring the #apple# if I have one.

scene first_work
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At first I counted #passes# because I feared losing them. | The first #cloth# I made had a #row# I could not stop staring at.
b : Do you still fear losing count? | Was the row poor?
a : Less now. The #numbers# keep me company. | Uneven. I kept the lesson and let the cloth go.

scene impatient_foot
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When I have to #wait#, my foot starts counting without me. | I can stand still, but my #numbers# will not.
b : Is that how I know you are restless? | What are you counting now?
a : Usually. I mean no offence by it. | The #steps# until the next thing begins.

scene enough_hands
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #loom# runs better when every #hand# has room to work. | I do not want a fine #bench# if another wolf is pushed out for it.
b : Would you turn down a better place? | How do you make room?
a : I would ask who else the #cloth# could employ. | Teach another #hand# what I have learned.

scene borrowed_hour
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A hard week makes me count each borrowed #coin#. | I have seen an #hour# of work traded for less than supper.
b : Can you save anything? | Does that make you angry?
a : A little, if the #boots# hold another season. | Yes. I keep the #count# so I can say why.

story two_missing_rows [topic=work self.age>=25]
  : I once finished a length of #cloth# and found two #rows# missing from my tally.
  : I checked the #edge# twice. The rows were there; my pencil had skipped them.
  ask : Would you have trusted the cloth or the page?
  b : I would have counted the cloth again.
  : That is what I did. The #count# in my head was right after all.

story waiting_game [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I made a game of counting the #steps# between the workroom and the road.
  : When a cart was late, I walked it until the #numbers# lost their meaning.
  ask : Would you have stayed by the door instead?
  b : I might have found something else to do.
  : I should have. The #shuttle# had work for me inside.

story brave_ending [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I heard a #tale# that ended with a wolf going back for a lost tool.
  : On the second telling, the wolf went back for another worker instead.
  ask : Which version would you tell again?
  b : The worker matters more than the tool.
  : I thought so. The #tale# was better the second time.

rule @bark_count
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Eight, nine... that is the #count#. | One more #row# before I stop.

rule @bark_apple
when concept=bark here.season=summer|autumn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That #apple# will do for a break. | I can smell #apple# fruit from here.

rule @bark_wait
when concept=bark here.time=day
does aside
cooldown 9h
say I can finish a #row# while we wait. | My #steps# are counting again.

rule @bark_rat
when concept=bark here.time=dusk|night
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Was that a #rat# behind the #bench#? | Close the #door# before the #rat# gets in.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Let me finish this #count#, then speak. | #greet#. I have an #hour# if you have a #tale#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You came back. Did the #tale# end well? | I remember our talk; sit by the #bench#.
dlg @1 resident.job : I work at the #loom# and keep the #rows# straight. | I count #passes# until a length of #cloth# is done.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Keep the #count# moving. | #saying.capitalize#. Come with another #tale#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you count under your breath? -> counting
node counting
say The #numbers# help me keep hold of the work. Sometimes they follow me home.
mood pleased
free
choice Does it ever go wrong? -> wrong
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
node wrong
say I once counted the #steps# to the wrong #door#. I laughed before anyone else could.
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
